        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e2d502d2-223a-564c-beeb-04131f170fa5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Languages: Kongo\n- Religions: Afro-American religions, African diasporic religions, New World traditions\n- Places: Brazil, Cuba, Haiti, Latin America, the Caribbean, the southern United States, the Americas, Africa\n- Concepts: creolized forms, ritual speech, traditional African religions, Christianity\n\nFacts:\n- Afro-American religions, also called African diasporic religions or New World traditions, developed in the Americas in various nations of Latin America, the Caribbean, and the southern United States.\n- Afro-American religions derive from traditional African religions of Africa with some influence from Christianity.\n- Kongo is still spoken in the above-mentioned countries, and creolized forms of Kongo are found in the ritual speech of Afro-American religions, especially in Brazil, Cuba, and Haiti.",
